<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:H/Au:N/C:C/I:C/A:C</cvss_vector>
<description>The version of Logstash installed on the remote host is 8.x prior to 8.19.14, 9.x prior to 9.2.8, or 9.3.x prior to 9.3.3. It is, therefore, affected by a path traversal vulnerability:

  - The archive extraction utilities used by Logstash do not properly validate file paths within compressed archives.
    An attacker who can serve a specially crafted archive to Logstash through a compromised or attacker-controlled     update endpoint can write arbitrary files to the host filesystem with the privileges of the Logstash process. In     certain configurations where automatic pipeline reloading is enabled, this can be escalated to remote code     execution. (CVE-2026-33466)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
<epss_score>0.0028</epss_score>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
<fname>logstash_esa_2026_29.nasl</fname>
<iavb>2026-B-0091</iavb>
<patch_publication_date>2026/04/08</patch_publication_date>
<plugin_modification_date>2026/04/10</plugin_modification_date>
