<ReportItem port="3269" svc_name="ldap" protocol="tcp" severity="0" pluginID="45410" pluginName="SSL Certificate &apos;commonName&apos; Mismatch" pluginFamily="General">
<description>The service running on the remote host presents an SSL certificate for which the &apos;commonName&apos; (CN) attribute does not match the hostname on which the service listens.</description>
<fname>ssl_cert_CN_mismatch.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2021/03/09</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>SSL Certificate &apos;commonName&apos; Mismatch</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2010/04/03</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.26</script_version>
<solution>If the machine has several names, make sure that users connect to the service through the DNS hostname that matches the common name in the certificate.</solution>
<synopsis>The &apos;commonName&apos; (CN) attribute in the SSL certificate does not match the hostname.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>
