<description>According to its self-reported version, Cisco IOS is affected by a vulnerability involving the Open Shortest Path First (OSPF) Routing Protocol Link State Advertisement (LSA) database. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can exploit this, by injecting crafted OSPF LSA type 1 packets, to cause the targeted router to flush its routing table and propagate the crafted OSPF LSA type 1 update through the OSPF AS domain, allowing the attacker to intercept or black-hole traffic.
Successful exploitation of this vulnerability requires that an attacker first accurately determine certain parameters within the LSA database on the target router.

Please see the included Cisco BIDs and Cisco Security Advisory for more information.

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
<epss_score>0.0052</epss_score>
