<description>According to its self-reported version and configuration, the Cisco IOS software running on the remote device is affected by a remote code execution vulnerability in the Cluster Management Protocol (CMP) subsystem due to improper handling of CMP-specific Telnet options. An unauthenticated, remote attacker can exploit this by establishing a Telnet session with malformed CMP-specific telnet options, to execute arbitrary code.</description>
