<ReportItem port="500" svc_name="ike" protocol="udp" severity="0" pluginID="62695" pluginName="IPSEC Internet Key Exchange (IKE) Version 2 Detection" pluginFamily="Service detection">
<asset_inventory>True</asset_inventory>
<description>The remote host seems to be enabled to do Internet Key Exchange (IKE).
This is typically indicative of a VPN server. VPN servers are used to connect remote hosts into internal resources.

Make sure that the use of this VPN endpoint is done in accordance with your corporate security policy.

Note that if the remote host is not configured to allow the Nessus host to perform IKE/IPSEC negotiations, Nessus won&apos;t be able to detect the IKE service.

Also note that this plugin does not run over IPv6.</description>
<fname>ike2_detect.nasl</fname>
<iavt>0001-T-0900</iavt>
<plugin_modification_date>2020/09/22</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>IPSEC Internet Key Exchange (IKE) Version 2 Detection</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2012/10/24</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.10</script_version>
<solution>If this service is not needed, disable it or filter incoming traffic to this port.</solution>
<synopsis>A VPN server is listening on the remote port.</synopsis>
<xref>IAVT:0001-T-0900</xref>
</ReportItem>
