<ReportItem port="113" svc_name="auth" protocol="tcp" severity="0" pluginID="10021" pluginName="Identd Service Detection" pluginFamily="Service detection">
<description>The remote host is running an ident (also known as &apos;auth&apos;) daemon.

The &apos;ident&apos; service provides sensitive information to potential attackers. It is designed to say which accounts are running which services. This helps attackers to focus on valuable services (those owned by root or other privileged accounts). If you do not use this service, and software you run does not require it, disable it.</description>
<fname>auth_enabled.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2011/03/11</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>Identd Service Detection</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>1999/06/22</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>$Revision: 1.32 $</script_version>
<solution>If you do not use this service and software you run does not require it, disable it.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote host is running an identification service.</synopsis>
</ReportItem>
