<ReportItem port="161" svc_name="snmp" protocol="udp" severity="0" pluginID="35296" pluginName="SNMP Protocol Version Detection" pluginFamily="SNMP">
<asset_inventory>True</asset_inventory>
<description>By sending an SNMP &apos;get-next-request&apos;, it is possible to determine the protocol version of the remote SNMP agent.</description>
<fname>snmp_version.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2019/11/22</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>SNMP Protocol Version Detection</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2009/01/06</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.12</script_version>
<see_also>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_Network_Management_Protocol</see_also>
<solution>Disable the SNMP service on the remote host if you do not use it, or filter incoming UDP packets going to this port.</solution>
<synopsis>This plugin reports the protocol version negotiated with the remote SNMP agent.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>
Nessus has negotiated SNMP communications at SNMPv2c.
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="161" svc_name="snmp" protocol="udp" severity="0" pluginID="185519" pluginName="SNMP Server Detection" pluginFamily="SNMP">
