<ReportItem port="161" svc_name="snmp" protocol="udp" severity="3" pluginID="41028" pluginName="SNMP Agent Default Community Name (public)" pluginFamily="SNMP">
<age_of_vuln>730 days +</age_of_vuln>
<bid>2112</bid>
<cve>CVE-1999-0517</cve>
<cvssV3_impactScore>5.2</cvssV3_impactScore>
<cvss_base_score>7.5</cvss_base_score>
<cvss_temporal_score>5.5</cvss_temporal_score>
<cvss_temporal_vector>CVSS2#E:U/RL:OF/RC:C</cvss_temporal_vector>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P</cvss_vector>
<description>It is possible to obtain the default community name of the remote SNMP server.

An attacker may use this information to gain more knowledge about the remote host, or to change the configuration of the remote system (if the default community allows such modifications).</description>
<epss_score>0.9243</epss_score>
<exploit_available>false</exploit_available>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
<exploitability_ease>No exploit is required</exploitability_ease>
<fname>snmp_default_public_community.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2022/06/01</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>SNMP Agent Default Community Name (public)</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2002/11/25</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<product_coverage>Low</product_coverage>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.14</script_version>
<solution>Disable the SNMP service on the remote host if you do not use it.
Either filter incoming UDP packets going to this port, or change the default community string.</solution>
<synopsis>The community name of the remote SNMP server can be guessed.</synopsis>
<thorough_tests>true</thorough_tests>
<threat_intensity_last_28>Very Low</threat_intensity_last_28>
<threat_recency>No recorded events</threat_recency>
<threat_sources_last_28>No recorded events</threat_sources_last_28>
<vpr_score>5.2</vpr_score>
<vuln_publication_date>1998/11/17</vuln_publication_date>
<plugin_output>
The remote SNMP server replies to the following default community
string :

public</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="9090" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="0" pluginID="10386" pluginName="Web Server No 404 Error Code Check" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<description>The remote web server is configured such that it does not return &apos;404 Not Found&apos; error codes when a nonexistent file is requested, perhaps returning instead a site map, search page or authentication page.

Nessus has enabled some counter measures for this.  However, they might be insufficient.  If a great number of security holes are produced for this port, they might not all be accurate.</description>
<fname>no404.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2022/06/17</plugin_modification_date>
