<description>According to its banner, the version of OpenSSH running on the remote host is prior to 7.6. It is, therefore, affected by a file creation restriction bypass vulnerability related to the &apos;process_open&apos; function in the file &apos;sftp-server.c&apos; that allows authenticated users to create zero-length files regardless of configuration.

