<description>The remote host is running the &apos;finger&apos; service. 

The purpose of this service is to show who is currently logged into the remote system, and to give information about the users of the remote system.  It provides useful information to attackers, since it allows them to gain usernames, determine how used a machine is, and see when each user logged in for the last time.</description>
