<description>The version of Tomcat installed on the remote host is prior to 8.5.34. It is, therefore, affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the fixed_in_apache_tomcat_8.5.34_security-8 advisory.

  - When the default servlet in Apache Tomcat versions 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.11, 8.5.0 to 8.5.33 and 7.0.23 to     7.0.90 returned a redirect to a directory (e.g. redirecting to &apos;/foo/&apos; when the user requested &apos;/foo&apos;) a     specially crafted URL could be used to cause the redirect to be generated to any URI of the attackers     choice. (CVE-2018-11784)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
