<description>It is possible to obtain the default community name of the remote SNMP server.

An attacker may use this information to gain more knowledge about the remote host, or to change the configuration of the remote system (if the default community allows such modifications).</description>
<epss_score>0.9243</epss_score>
<exploit_available>false</exploit_available>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
