<ReportItem port="161" svc_name="snmp" protocol="udp" severity="2" pluginID="76474" pluginName="SNMP &apos;GETBULK&apos; Reflection DDoS" pluginFamily="SNMP">
<age_of_vuln>730 days +</age_of_vuln>
<cve>CVE-2008-4309</cve>
<cvssV3_impactScore>3.6</cvssV3_impactScore>
<cvss_base_score>5.0</cvss_base_score>
<cvss_score_source>CVE-2008-4309</cvss_score_source>
<cvss_temporal_score>3.7</cvss_temporal_score>
<cvss_temporal_vector>CVSS2#E:U/RL:OF/RC:C</cvss_temporal_vector>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:N/A:P</cvss_vector>
<description>The remote SNMP daemon is responding with a large amount of data to a &apos;GETBULK&apos; request with a larger than normal value for &apos;max-repetitions&apos;. A remote attacker can use this SNMP server to conduct a reflected distributed denial of service attack on an arbitrary remote host.</description>
<epss_score>0.0787</epss_score>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
<exploited_by_nessus>true</exploited_by_nessus>
<fname>snmp_getbulk_reflection_ddos.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2023/11/08</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>SNMP &apos;GETBULK&apos; Reflection DDoS</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2014/07/11</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<product_coverage>Low</product_coverage>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.9</script_version>
<see_also>http://www.nessus.org/u?8b551b5c</see_also>
<solution>Disable the SNMP service on the remote host if you do not use it.
Otherwise, restrict and monitor access to this service, and consider changing the default &apos;public&apos; community string.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote SNMP daemon is affected by a vulnerability that allows a reflected distributed denial of service attack.</synopsis>
<threat_intensity_last_28>Very Low</threat_intensity_last_28>
<threat_recency>No recorded events</threat_recency>
<threat_sources_last_28>No recorded events</threat_sources_last_28>
<vpr_score>3.6</vpr_score>
<plugin_output>
Nessus was able to determine the SNMP service can be abused in an SNMP
Reflection DDoS attack :

