<cvss_temporal_vector>CVSS2#E:U/RL:ND/RC:C</cvss_temporal_vector>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N</cvss_vector>
<description>The remote host supports the use of RC4 in one or more cipher suites.
The RC4 cipher is flawed in its generation of a pseudo-random stream of bytes so that a wide variety of small biases are introduced into the stream, decreasing its randomness.

If plaintext is repeatedly encrypted (e.g., HTTP cookies), and an attacker is able to obtain many (i.e., tens of millions) ciphertexts, the attacker may be able to derive the plaintext.</description>
<epss_score>0.9076</epss_score>
<exploit_available>false</exploit_available>
<exploit_code_maturity>Unproven</exploit_code_maturity>
<exploitability_ease>No known exploits are available</exploitability_ease>
<fname>ssl_rc4_supported_ciphers.nasl</fname>
<in_the_news>true</in_the_news>
<plugin_modification_date>2025/05/09</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>SSL RC4 Cipher Suites Supported (Bar Mitzvah)</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2013/04/05</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<product_coverage>Very High</product_coverage>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
