<description>The version of MongoDB installed on the remote host is 7.0 prior to 7.0.31, 8.0 prior to 8.0.20, 8.2 prior to 8.2.6, and 8.3.0-rc0. It is, therefore, affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the SERVER-118849 advisory.

  - A specially crafted aggregation query with $lookup by an authenticated user with write privileges can     cause a double-free or use-after-free memory issue in the slot-based execution (SBE) engine when an     in-memory hash table is spilled to disk. (CVE-2026-4358)

  Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version   number.</description>
