<description>The instance of MongoDB running on the remote host is affected by MongoBleed, an unauthenticated unintialized heap memory leak vulnerability:

  - Mismatched length fields in Zlib compressed protocol headers may allow a read of uninitialized heap memory by an     unauthenticated client. (CVE-2025-14847)

A remote, unauthenticated attacker can exploit this issue, via a specially crafted request, to leak potentially sensitive server memory.</description>
