<ReportItem port="1434" svc_name="ms-sql-m?" protocol="udp" severity="0" pluginID="10674" pluginName="Microsoft SQL Server UDP Query Remote Version Disclosure" pluginFamily="Databases">
<cpe>cpe:/a:microsoft:sql_server</cpe>
<description>Microsoft SQL server has a function wherein remote users can query the database server for the version that is being run.  The query takes place over the same UDP port that handles the mapping of multiple SQL server instances on the same machine. 

It is important to note that, after Version 8.00.194, Microsoft decided not to update this function.  This means that the data returned by the SQL ping is inaccurate for newer releases of SQL Server.</description>
<fname>mssql_ping.nasl</fname>
<plugin_modification_date>2018/03/13</plugin_modification_date>
<plugin_name>Microsoft SQL Server UDP Query Remote Version Disclosure</plugin_name>
<plugin_publication_date>2001/05/25</plugin_publication_date>
<plugin_type>remote</plugin_type>
<risk_factor>None</risk_factor>
<script_version>1.29</script_version>
<solution>If there is only a single SQL instance installed on the remote host, consider filter incoming traffic to this port.</solution>
<synopsis>It is possible to determine the remote SQL server version.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>
