<description>The remote SNMP daemon is responding with a large amount of data to a &apos;GETBULK&apos; request with a larger than normal value for &apos;max-repetitions&apos;. A remote attacker can use this SNMP server to conduct a reflected distributed denial of service attack on an arbitrary remote host.</description>
